      'For a small company or micro-enterprise in France, the requirements are phased:\n\n- **From 1 September 2026:** You must be able to **receive** electronic invoices, regardless of company size.[2][3]\n- **From 1 September 2027:** You must **issue e-invoices** for in-scope domestic B2B transactions and meet applicable **e-reporting** obligations, including for relevant B2C or cross-border transactions.[2][3][9]\n- **How invoices are handled:** In-scope e-invoices must use a structured format and be sent through a French-approved platform; an emailed PDF alone is not considered a compliant e-invoice.[2][4]\n- **Scope and exceptions:** The rules generally concern businesses established in France and transactions subject to French VAT. Some VAT-exempt activities are excluded. The specific treatment can depend on your activity and transactions.[1][10]\n\nIn practice, small businesses should arrange a way to receive electronic invoices by September 2026, then prepare for issuing and reporting by September 2027.',
