        title: 'France pauses e-invoicing penalties until end of 2026 | VATfaqs.com',
        snippet:
          '# France pauses e-invoicing penalties until end of 2026  \nFrance has announced that no penalties will be applied for non-compliance with the e-invoicing reform during 2026, as authorities focus on supporting businesses through the transition period. The e-invoicing mandate itself went live on 1 September 2026 for large and medium-sized companies, with SMEs and micro-enterprises required to comply from 1 September 2027. Cybersecurity measures for approved platforms are also being enforced.  \nKey Takeaways  \n- From 1 September 2026: French e-invoicing mandate goes live for large and medium-sized companies, requiring electronic invoices via an approved platform and e-reporting obligations\n- From 1 September 2026: Approved platforms must submit a cybersecurity progress report before the end of September 2026, report incidents to authorities, and conduct penetration testing beginning in autumn 2026\n## Key Insights  \n### When does the French e-invoicing mandate become effective for large and medium-sized companies?  \nFrom 1 September 2026, large and medium-sized French companies must issue electronic invoices via an approved platform and comply with e-reporting obligations.\n### When are small and medium enterprises required to comply with the French e-invoicing mandate?  \nFrom 1 September 2027, small and medium enterprises and micro-enterprises in France must issue electronic invoices and meet e-reporting obligations.',
