        snippet:
          'All businesses must be able to receive eInvoices since 1 September 2026 and issue eInvoices from 1 September 2027. Large and medium-sized companies must be able to issue eInvoices via a government-approved platform from 1 September 2026, as ...\nB2G electronic invoicing (eInvoicing) is mandatory for all public procurement transactions via the Chorus Pro platform · B2B mandate: B2B eInvoicing will become mandatory in phases. All businesses must be able to receive eInvoices since 1 September 2026 and issue eInvoices from 1 September 2027. Large and medium-sized companies must be able to issue eInvoices via a government-approved platform from 1 September 2026, as mandated by Article 91 of Law No.\nVAT Real-Time Reporting: Starting 1 September 2026, France will require the biggest VAT-registered companies, including certain foreign entities, to submit detailed transaction data for B2C and cross-border transactions directly to tax authorities through approved platforms. The smallest companies will have to comply with this obligation on 1 September 2027. Monitoring mechanism: The monitoring mechanism tracks uptake and usage; in 2023, Chorus Pro processed over 78 million invoices from around 910,000 suppliers and over 160,000 public entities.\nStarting 1 September 2026, France will introduce, at first for the biggest companies, a mandatory real-time reporting system, expanding its existing eInvoicing mandate. This update requires VAT-registered companies in France to transmit detailed transaction data for Business-to-Consumer (B2C) and cross-border transactions directly to French tax authorities, enhancing the digital taxation landscape.\nLarge and medium businesses must issue eInvoices via a government-approved platform from 1 September 2026 and the obligation extends to remaining businesses on 1 September 2027. In parallel, the government will expand the eReporting system to include B2C and cross-border transactions, with invoice and payment data transmitted through certified private intermediaries.',
